From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:25:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox, settings_ui: the host view's identity layer
 and Hide the Disks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

docs/HOST-VIEW-EXTRA-LAYER.md §4.4, the Zeo side of step 1 (operator,
2026-11-23: "default, plus an extra layer"; the overlay behind its own
switch, off until a real build's cost is measured).

ai-jail 3.5.0-r3 (the fork's feat/host-view-extra) adds an identity layer
under --mask-host -- the kernel's build strings without suffix or date, a
generic os-release, a swap table with no swap, a boot id of the jail's
own, a time namespace that starts CLOCK_BOOTTIME and sysinfo().uptime at
the launch, CPU topology files for lscpu -- and a new --overlay-system:
/usr, /etc and /opt through read-only overlays, so the mount table names
no host disk for them.

What changes here:
- probe.rs reads --overlay-system from ai-jail --help
  (supports_overlay_system). It ships with the identity layer, so it also
  says that layer is there; there is no flag for the layer itself, which
  rides --mask-host.
- host_view::host_args_for(mask_host, HostLayer, exists): under mask_host
  with the identity layer, /proc/swaps and the boot id are no longer
  masked (IDENTITY_LAYER_MASKS). Zeo's --mask lands after ai-jail's view,
  so an empty mask would replace the header-only swap table and the
  jail's own boot id. The other 0159 masks stay: older binaries need them
  and a path masked twice costs nothing. --overlay-system follows
  --mask-host when the project asks for it. host_args() keeps its old
  behaviour (no layer) for callers that do not know the binary.
- agent_sandbox.overlay_system (default false, per project like
  mask_host). It applies only with mask_host: launch.rs asks for it as
  `mask_host && overlay_system_for_key`. A project that asks for it from
  an ai-jail without --overlay-system is refused
  (LaunchCause::OverlaySystemUnsupported, cause=overlay_system_unsupported),
  as 0146 refuses --mask-host. The settings fingerprint includes it, so
  the restart notice fires when it changes.
- The Agent Sandbox page's Host section: "Hide the Disks"
  (set_project_overlay_system), disabled with "Applies only while Hide
  the Host is on." when the host is shown; Hide the Host's note now says
  what stays visible (the writable folders' disk and size, CPU numbers,
  cpuid, toolchain version strings). The page's command preview passes
  the overlay too and lists every mask (it cannot probe the binary).

Why off by default: an overlay slows metadata walks (+21 % on a find
over /usr, measured 2026-11-23); a cargo build has not been measured.
The overlay also fails with EINVAL where the root is already an
overlayfs stacked too deep (the lab's containers) -- ai-jail reports it
and the jail does not start, which is why it is a choice, not a default.

Tests:
- host_view_tests: host_view_identity_layer_takes_over_swap_and_the_boot_id,
  host_view_overlay_system_rides_mask_host_only.
- host_view_layer_tests (new, fake ai-jail whose --help lists
  --overlay-system or not): the overlay follows --mask-host; refused
  without the option, naming it; off by default; not asked for without
  the host view; swap and boot id left to the layer, kept for an older
  binary.
- settings_ui agent_jail_host_tests:
  agent_jail_host_disks_follow_the_project_and_need_the_host_view, and
  the existing switch test extended with the two new fields.
---

diff --git a/assets/settings/default.json b/assets/settings/default.json
index 6f2ada6..050c6f0 100644
--- a/assets/settings/default.json
+++ b/assets/settings/default.json
@@ -3201,6 +3201,9 @@
     // On by default (operator, 2026-11-22: hide the host from the jailed agent); it also
     // reserves the jail's cores, which its CPU files must match.
     "mask_host": true,
+    // Also serve /usr, /etc and /opt through read-only overlays under the host view, so the
+    // mount table names no host disk for them (ai-jail --overlay-system). Slower metadata walks.
+    "overlay_system": false,
     // Whether jailed agents load the account's claude.ai connectors, which reach their
     // vendors through anthropic.com, past `allow_hosts`.
     "claude_ai_connectors": false,
